      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T04:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Global uniqueness within a document is guaranteed by the daemon, which is the condition this comment asks for.\n\nCollaborativeEditing::AwarenessPeer carries an owner field, set to the account that first announced a given client id in a given document. onAwarenessMessage() refuses an entry whose client id is already owned by a different member, so two peers cannot hold the same client id in the same document: the second claimant is dropped, not merged.\n\nThat check exists precisely because an authorised member picks its own client ids and could otherwise speak for another\u0027s. Keying on peerId as well would therefore not remove a collision -- it would only hide the fact that one was already refused upstream.",
      "revId": "89f378d41fc5c4c77d29e9e3a4e324cc51f43227",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
