      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T04:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The precision concern does not apply here: no client id can exist outside the range JavaScript represents exactly. It is bounded twice, on both sides.\n\nOn emission, CollaborativeEditing::replicaId() draws from [1, 2^53-1], with the reason in the code: \"the yjs ecosystem carries these ids through JSON, where integers above 2^53 are no longer exact\".\n\nOn reception, the lib0 decoder refuses to produce a larger value at all -- y_protocol.cpp defines MAX_SAFE_INTEGER as (1 \u003c\u003c 53) - 1 and readVarUint() fails the frame rather than truncating it. A peer announcing a client id above that range is rejected before it ever reaches the signal, let alone QML.\n\nThat bound is not ours: it is what yjs itself relies on, since its client ids travel through JSON. Converting to a string would add a conversion at every cursor update to widen a domain nothing can leave.",
      "revId": "89f378d41fc5c4c77d29e9e3a4e324cc51f43227",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    }
